      ]
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N02",
      "text": "Thirty years later, early orbital rockets still looked like fragile metal pencils. In nineteen fifty-seven, Vanguard lifted four feet before collapsing into flames. Weeks later, Juno One reached orbit by spinning an exposed tub of eleven miniature rocket tubes bolted to its nose.",
      "delivery": "MEASURED_EVIDENCE",
      "rate": "-1%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
