        "tubes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "N03",
      "text": "By nineteen sixty-two, NASA's Mercury-Atlas gleamed like solid steel\u2014yet its tank walls were thinner than a dime. Left unpressurized, the entire rocket would crumple under its own weight, dropping two side boosters mid-sky as it climbed.",
      "delivery": "SCIENTIFIC_WONDER",
      "rate": "-1%",
      "pitch": "-1Hz",
